  Error · Duplicate operationId (1) [duplicate-operation-id]
    Why it matters: An operationId must be unique in the document, and this documentation turns it into the operation's deep link: one of the two links lands on the other operation.
    How to fix: Rename one of the operationIds so that each value is unique in the document — a verb and a noun reads best (listPets, getPet).
    - operationId “getPet” is used by more than one operation.
      GET /pet/{petId} · /paths/~1pet~1{petId}/get

Docs readiness — 74 %

  Warning · Security scheme without description (1) [security-scheme-described]
    Why it matters: The credentials block shows that description to explain what to paste and where to get it. Without one, the reader faces a bare field labelled with the scheme's key.
    How to fix: Add a description to the scheme saying where to get the credential and in what form to paste it.
    - Security scheme “apiKey” has no description.
      components.securitySchemes.apiKey · /components/securitySchemes/apiKey

  Note · Operation without tag (1) [operation-tagged]
    Why it matters: It lands in the navigation's catch-all group along with every other untagged operation, and the reader cannot tell which family it belongs to.
    How to fix: Add at least one tag, and declare it with a description in the top-level tags list.
